  "description": "Your first consonant rows: క ఖ గ ఘ and చ ఛ జ ఝ — every one carries a hidden అ.",
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "u83-i01",
      "te": "క",
      "audioTe": "క. కారు.",
      "gloss": "ka — as in 'kaaru' (car)",
      "words": [{ "te": "క", "gloss": "ka — a plain consonant always carries the అ sound inside" }],
      "tags": ["consonant"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "distractors": ["u83-i02"],
      "note": "క alone already reads 'ka' — the అ is built in. That's why Telugu needs no letter between క and ల to write కల."
    },
    {
      "id": "u83-i02",
      "te": "ఖ",
      "audioTe": "ఖ. ఖర్చు.",
      "gloss": "kha — as in 'kharchu' (expense)",
      "words": [{ "te": "ఖ", "gloss": "kha — క with a puff of breath" }],
      "tags": ["consonant"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "distractors": ["u83-i01"],
      "note": "Aspirated letters like ఖ are just their plain twin plus a burst of air: క → ఖ."
    },
    {
      "id": "u83-i03",
      "te": "గ",
      "audioTe": "గ. గది.",
      "gloss": "ga — as in 'gadi' (room)",
